~ examples.wit — three complete documents in wildly different shapes, all in
~ Wit. Thesis is open by default; the creative-writing and RPG panels fold out
~ on click (wired in script.wit). Each panel shows real Wit source and what it
~ renders to. Exposed as #page_examples.

#page_examples
@section |class section| |id examples|
  @div(class wrap)
    @h2 Three documents, one language h2@
    @p(class lead) A journal-style thesis, a novel that never indents, and a branching game script — same tool, same source rules. Click a panel to open it. p@

    @div(class examples)
      @div |class example open|
        @div(class example-head)
          @div(class example-title) 🎓 A thesis chapter div@
          @div(class example-badge) Academic div@
          @div(class example-toggle) Collapse ↑ div@
        div@
        @div(class example-body)
          @div(class demo-pane)
            @div(class demo-label) Wit source div@
            @div(class demo-src)
              @@@pre
reference ./sources.wit        ~ the bibliography, written once

@h2 3 · Method 3.method@

We pre-train on a masked-language objective, following
@cite bert bert@, then fine-tune each task in turn.

@figure
  @img |src corpus.png| |alt Corpus by domain|
  @figcaption Figure 3.1 — Corpus composition. figcaption@
figure@

@table
  |schema [split, docs, tokens]|
  |rows @corpus|
table@

As @xref 3.method xref@ shows, scale beats architecture —
a point @cite sutton sutton@ makes forcefully.
pre@@@
            div@
          div@
          @div(class demo-pane)
            @div(class demo-label) Renders to div@
            @div(class demo-out)
              @h2 3 · Method h2@
              We pre-train on a masked-language objective, following @strong Devlin et al. strong@ (2019), then fine-tune each task in turn.

              @table |rows [[Split, Documents, Tokens], [Train, 40k, 12.4M], [Dev, 5k, 1.5M], [Test, 5k, 1.5M]]|
              @aside(class note) Table 3.1 — Corpus statistics by split. aside@

              As @strong §3 strong@ shows, scale beats architecture — a point @strong Sutton strong@ (2019) makes forcefully.

              @h3 References h3@
              @ul
                @li Devlin, J. et al. (2019). BERT. @em NAACL em@. li@
                @li Sutton, R. (2019). The Bitter Lesson. li@
              ul@
            div@
          div@
          @div(class demo-vs) @strong Why not LaTeX? strong@ the citation, the table, and the cross-reference all resolve from one source — no preamble, no package hunt, no re-compile roulette. div@
        div@
      div@

      @div |class example|
        @div(class example-head)
          @div(class example-title) ✍ A novel that never indents div@
          @div(class example-badge) Prose div@
          @div(class example-toggle) Expand ↓ div@
        div@
        @div(class example-body)
          @div(class demo-pane)
            @div(class demo-label) Wit source — flat, no indentation div@
            @div(class demo-src)
              @@@pre
@h2 One · The Harbour h2@

The rain had not stopped for three days.

Mara pressed her palm to the cold glass and counted
the boats that were no longer there. @em One. Two. em@
The third had been her father's.

@break ✦ ✦ ✦ break@

"You can't stay," the harbourmaster said.

She said nothing. There was nothing, she had learned,
that saying could fix.
pre@@@
            div@
          div@
          @div(class demo-pane)
            @div(class demo-label) Renders to div@
            @div(class demo-out)
              @h2 One · The Harbour h2@
              The rain had not stopped for three days.

              Mara pressed her palm to the cold glass and counted the boats that were no longer there. @em One. Two. em@ The third had been her father's.

              @div(class break) ✦ ✦ ✦ div@

              "You can't stay," the harbourmaster said.

              She said nothing. There was nothing, she had learned, that saying could fix.
            div@
          div@
          @div(class demo-vs) @strong Why not Markdown? strong@ for pure prose Wit gets out of the way entirely — but a scene break, an epigraph, or a chapter component is one node away, not a drop into raw HTML. div@
        div@
      div@

      @div |class example|
        @div(class example-head)
          @div(class example-title) 🎲 A branching game script div@
          @div(class example-badge) Interactive div@
          @div(class example-toggle) Expand ↓ div@
        div@
        @div(class example-body)
          @div(class demo-pane)
            @div(class demo-label) Wit source — data, conditions, iteration div@
            @div(class demo-src)
              @@@pre
#hero: { name - Vera, hp - 8, gold - 12 } !!

@scene The Crossroads scene@

::hero.name::, the road forks beneath a broken
signpost. You are carrying ::hero.gold:: gold.

(if @hero.hp is low)
@warn You are wounded — the dark path may kill you. warn@
(end)

@choices
  @choice |goto village| Take the lit path choice@
  @choice |goto tower|   Take the dark path choice@
choices@

Pack: (each @hero.pack) ::this::  (end)
pre@@@
            div@
          div@
          @div(class demo-pane)
            @div(class demo-label) Renders to (one playthrough) div@
            @div(class demo-out)
              @h3 The Crossroads h3@
              @strong Vera strong@, the road forks beneath a broken signpost. You are carrying 12 gold.

              @aside(class note) ⚔ You are wounded — the dark path may kill you. aside@

              @strong Choose: strong@
              @ul
                @li → Take the @em lit em@ path toward the village li@
                @li → Take the @em dark em@ path toward the tower li@
              ul@

              @em Pack: em@ torch · rope · a letter you should have burned.
            div@
          div@
          @div(class demo-vs) @strong Why not HTML? strong@ the stats, the wounded-check, and the inventory are data and logic in the document — not a wall of tags you hand-edit for every state. div@
        div@
      div@

    div@
  div@
section@
page_examples#
